            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for face to face, then the Latin for by which way."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: simul",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "simul — \"at the same time\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "simul is inherited, usually traced to the Proto-Indo-European root sem-, \"one, together\". Greek hama, \"together\", is a cousin (Lewis & Short), and so is English same."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
